Written Description - including why a PUD is necessary
Per discussions with staff and changes in development conditions, PUD amendment to update land use plan, phasing, & simplyfy PUD text
The following review criteria are found in the UDC regarding a Planned
Development - Regulating Plan or Development Master Plan. Please
acknowledge the proposed application meets each review criterion by
checking the box.
The application meets all threshold requirements for application of the PUD District or Form-based Code standards (2.2.2.d.1)

The application presents clear and specific criteria on how the property and subsequent development will be reviewed, regulated and modified consistent with
these regulations (2.2.2.d.2).

The application is in accordance with the development policies and physical patterns identified in the Comprehensive Plan (2.2.2.d.3).

The application reflects sound planning and urban design principles with respect to existing and potential future development in the vicinity, including
consideration of current and future streets, open spaces, blocks and lots, and public utilities or facilities (2.2.2.d.4).

The application meets the purposes, intent, and all applicable standards in Article 4 (2.2.2.d.5).

Any phasing proposed in the application is clearly indicated and demonstrates a logical and well-planned development pattern. This may include consideration
of amenities and public facilities of the subdivision within each phase compared to the anticipated timing or the likelihood of future phases being constructed
as planned (2.2.2.d.6).

The impacts identified in specific studies or technical reports that were prepared or requested to be prepared in association with the application, and whether
the findings and recommendations of these reports, or any modifications or conditions on approval of the application, can mitigate these impacts (2.2.2.d.7).
